5. Correct Retry Schedule

Assumption: four total CRM attempts, consisting of the initial call plus three retries.

Attempt 1: Call immediately
    │ failure: 429/504
    ▼
Wait 1 second

Attempt 2: Retry
    │ failure: 429/504
    ▼
Wait 2 seconds

Attempt 3: Retry
    │ failure: 429/504
    ▼
Wait 4 seconds

Attempt 4: Final retry
    │
    ├── 200/206 ──► Return success
    └── 429/504 ──► Return final failure

Total retries       : 3
Total CRM attempts  : 4
Total planned wait  : 1 + 2 + 4 = 7 seconds


The CRM request duration must be added separately. Therefore, the earlier fixed “14 seconds” timeline is not reliable unless every mock request intentionally takes a specified amount of time.

6. HTTP Handling Matrix
Status   Meaning              Retry?   Workflow action
---------------------------------------------------------------
200      Success              No       Return complete data
206      Partial content      No       Return available data
400      Invalid request      No       Return validation error
404      Customer not found   No       Return not-found error
429      Rate limited         Yes      Honor Retry-After/backoff
504      Gateway timeout      Yes      Apply exponential backoff


For a 429 response, prefer the server-provided Retry-After value when available rather than always waiting only 1, 2, and 4 seconds.

